//! lotus/stereo_reverb.rye — ALES187: the REVERB carried into stereo — ALES186's Schroeder network run on BOTH channels with the SAME
//! comb-and-allpass bank, each channel reverbed through ITS OWN network — the wing's keystone made stereo. ALES186 seated the mono reverb
//! (parallel combs summed then diffused through series allpasses, wet = series_allpass(sum of parallel combs(dry))); a reverb is heard in a
//! room and a room has two ears, so carrying it into stereo is the natural next rung, exactly as the stereo comb (echo, ALES181), the
//! stereo multi-tap (ALES183), and the stereo allpass (ALES185) were carried before it — each ran a proven mono stage on both channels with
//! one shared set of knobs. The reverb is one more mono stage; this is that same faithful carry over the keystone.
//!
//! The crux — the SAME bank on BOTH channels, each through ITS OWN network, is the linked stereo reverb: both reverberant tails settle in
//! lockstep, the image held in time. The combs and allpasses are counts of sample indices and named fractions the caller NAMES, not scalars
//! measured across the field, so the same bank on each channel gives each ear the same room. Mono `reverb` runs every comb on a copy of its
//! OWN clip and diffuses its OWN comb-bank sum, so run once per channel the left reverberates the left's audio and the right the right's,
//! never crossed — NO cross-channel read.
//!
//! HONESTLY NOTED — like the feedback echo (ALES181), the flanger (ALES180), and the allpass (ALES185), and UNLIKE the snapshot rungs, the
//! reverb's combs and allpasses read their delayed OUTPUT through a `@divTrunc` recirculation, so an exact panned integer ratio does NOT
//! survive (the feedback truncation drifts it). The image law proven here is therefore the identical-channel one — a centred master staying
//! identical through the reverb, the sense a mix cares about — not the stronger both-cases ratio the linear snapshot rungs earn.
//!
//! The rule, stated once: validate the whole bank and span ONCE against the shared length up front (ALES186's own `precheck`) — refuse
//! NoCombs, TooManyStages, BadDelay, BadGain, and BadRange BEFORE either channel is touched, so a refusal never reverbs one channel and
//! leaves the other torn; then run ALES186's `reverb` on each channel with the SAME bank.
//!
//! The crux — three laws. THE STEREO REVERB LAW: each channel equals ALES186's mono `reverb` with the SAME bank over the same span byte for
//! byte, proven side by side with genuinely different per-channel content — the left reverbed by the left's samples, the right by the
//! right's, never crossed. THE IDENTICAL-CHANNEL IMAGE LAW: a centred master (both channels equal) stays identical through the reverb. THE
//! SILENCE / BALANCE / ATOMICITY / DEGENERATE LAW: an all-silent master reverbs to silence on both; left.len == right.len after; an empty
//! bank, an over-long bank, a bad delay, a bad gain, and an out-of-range span each refuse by name with BOTH channels untouched and still
//! balanced; count = 0 the identity on both.
//!
//! Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES187.
//! Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-093859_fill-ales187-lotus-stereo-reverb.md
//! Stands on: lotus/reverb.rye (ALES186) — the mono reverb run once per channel, its ReverbError reused whole and its `precheck` reused for
//! the up-front atomic validation; lotus/pan.rye (ALES10) — the StereoClip and its balance invariant; lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2) — the Clip
//! the mono reverb composes over.
//!
//! HONEST SCOPE — software only, purely LOCAL. Two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right), each reverbed through ALES186's own bounded
//! network (bounded whole-clip comb copies, a bounded saturating comb-bank sum, each allpass's bounded snapshot), siloed to lotus/. It
//! changes sample VALUES only, never a length; the two channels leave balanced. The delays are counts of sample INDICES, not milliseconds
//! against a clock (a real-time stereo twin through the ALES5 clock is a later rung, exactly as stereo_echo_time followed stereo_echo); the
//! feedbacks and gains are named fractions, not room sizes in seconds. No cross-channel read, no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no
//! funds, no real device, no real speaker.
//!
//!   env RYE_ZIG=vendor/zig-toolchain/zig rye/bin/rye run lotus/stereo_reverb.rye selftest

const std = @import("std");
const assert = std.debug.assert;
const print = std.debug.print;

const timeline = @import("timeline.rye");
const pan = @import("pan.rye");
const reverb = @import("reverb.rye");

pub const stereo_reverb_version = "20260815.093859";

/// The stereo reverb's faults are exactly ALES186's own `ReverbError` — `NoCombs`, `TooManyStages`, `BadDelay`, `BadGain`, and `BadRange` —
/// reused by name, since carrying the reverb into stereo adds no new fault: it validates one shared bank and span against the shared length,
/// then runs the same mono reverb on each channel.
pub const StereoReverbError = reverb.ReverbError;

/// Reverberate `count` samples starting at `start` in BOTH channels of `sc` with the SAME comb-and-allpass bank — each channel Schroeder's
/// network wet = series_allpass(sum of parallel combs(dry)) — by running ALES186's proven mono `reverb` on each channel. The shared bank
/// preserves the stereo image: a centred master stays identical through the reverb (an exact panned ratio does NOT survive — the feedback
/// truncation drifts it, like the echo, flanger, and allpass). Each channel reverberates its OWN audio — no cross-channel read. Validates
/// the whole bank and span ONCE against the shared length before either channel is touched (ALES186's `precheck`): refuses NoCombs,
/// TooManyStages, BadDelay, BadGain, and BadRange, both channels untouched. Values only — never the length; the two channels leave balanced.
pub fn stereo_reverb(
    sc: *pan.StereoClip,
    start: u32,
    count: u32,
    combs: []const reverb.CombSpec,
    allpasses: []const reverb.AllpassSpec,
) StereoReverbError!void {
    // invariant: the two channels enter balanced — the defining StereoClip invariant, the ground the shared bank preserves.
    assert(sc.left.len == sc.right.len);
    // invariant: the whole bank and span are legal against the SHARED length — checked before any write, so a refusal never reverbs one channel and leaves the other torn.
    const len: u32 = sc.left.len;
    try reverb.precheck(len, start, count, combs, allpasses);

    // Every check passed and holds identically for both channels (same bank, same span, shared length), so each mono reverb is
    // pre-validated to succeed — no refusal can land between the two channel edits. The SAME bank on each channel, each reverberating its
    // OWN audio, never the other's.
    try reverb.reverb(&sc.left, start, count, combs, allpasses);
    try reverb.reverb(&sc.right, start, count, combs, allpasses);

    // invariant: the channels leave balanced — a reverb writes values only, so each channel holds its starting length and the stereo image stays aligned in time.
    assert(sc.left.len == len and sc.right.len == len);
    assert(sc.left.len <= sc.left.buf.len and sc.right.len <= sc.right.buf.len);
}

// --- selftest: THE STEREO REVERB LAW — each channel equals ALES186's mono reverb with the SAME bank byte for byte, different per-channel
//     content; THE IDENTICAL-CHANNEL IMAGE LAW — a centred master stays identical; THE SILENCE / BALANCE / ATOMICITY / DEGENERATE LAW —
//     silence to silence, balanced, each of five refusals untouched, count 0 identity

fn eq(got: []const i16, want: []const i16) bool {
    if (got.len != want.len) return false;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    while (i < want.len) : (i += 1) if (got[i] != want[i]) return false;
    return true;
}

fn load_stereo(sc: *pan.StereoClip, l: []const i16, r: []const i16) !void {
    try timeline.splice(&sc.left, 0, l);
    try timeline.splice(&sc.right, 0, r);
}

fn run_selftest() !u8 {
    const combs = [_]reverb.CombSpec{ .{ .delay = 2, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 }, .{ .delay = 3, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 3 } };
    const allpasses = [_]reverb.AllpassSpec{.{ .delay = 2, .num = 1, .den = 2 }};

    // 1. THE STEREO REVERB LAW — each channel equals ALES186's mono reverb with the SAME bank, proven side by side over one span with
    //    genuinely different per-channel content: the left reverbed by the left's samples, the right by the right's, never crossed.
    {
        const ll = [_]i16{ 8000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
        const rr = [_]i16{ 0, 0, 6000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &ll, &rr);
        try stereo_reverb(&sc, 0, 8, &combs, &allpasses);

        var ml = timeline.Clip{};
        try timeline.splice(&ml, 0, &ll);
        try reverb.reverb(&ml, 0, 8, &combs, &allpasses);
        var mr = timeline.Clip{};
        try timeline.splice(&mr, 0, &rr);
        try reverb.reverb(&mr, 0, 8, &combs, &allpasses);

        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), ml.samples())) return error.LeftReverbNotMono;
        if (!eq(sc.right.samples(), mr.samples())) return error.RightReverbNotMono;
        // the two channels genuinely differ — the left is not the right rung, proving no crossing
        if (eq(sc.left.samples(), sc.right.samples())) return error.ChannelsDidNotDiffer;
    }

    // 2. THE IDENTICAL-CHANNEL IMAGE LAW — a centred master (both channels equal) stays identical through the reverb. Honestly noted: an
    //    exact panned ratio does NOT survive (the delayed-output @divTrunc drifts it, like the echo, flanger, and allpass), so only the
    //    centred image is claimed — the sense a mix cares about.
    {
        const same = [_]i16{ 8000, -3000, 0, 2000, 0, 0, -1000, 0 };
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &same, &same);
        try stereo_reverb(&sc, 0, 8, &combs, &allpasses);
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), sc.right.samples())) return error.IdentityChannelsSplit;
    }

    // 3a. THE SILENCE / BALANCE / LENGTH LAW — an all-silent master reverbs to silence on both; the channels stay equal length and each
    //     holds its starting length.
    {
        var sc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&sc, &[_]i16{ 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 }, &[_]i16{ 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 });
        try stereo_reverb(&sc, 0, 8, &combs, &allpasses);
        const zeros = [_]i16{ 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
        if (!eq(sc.left.samples(), &zeros) or !eq(sc.right.samples(), &zeros)) return error.SilenceWrong;

        var bc = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&bc, &[_]i16{ 8000, -8000, 200, -9000, 3000, -3000, 100, -100 }, &[_]i16{ -400, 3000, -700, 5000, 600, -600, 800, -800 });
        try stereo_reverb(&bc, 0, 8, &combs, &allpasses);
        if (bc.left.len != bc.right.len) return error.Unbalanced;
        if (bc.left.len != 8) return error.LengthChanged;
    }

    // 3b. THE ATOMICITY LAW — an empty bank (NoCombs), an over-long bank (TooManyStages), a bad delay, a bad gain (at unity), and an
    //     out-of-range span each refuse by name with BOTH channels byte for byte untouched and still balanced.
    {
        const tl = [_]i16{ 5, -6, 7, -8 };
        const tr = [_]i16{ -7, 6, -5, 4 };

        var n = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&n, &tl, &tr);
        const nocombs = [_]reverb.CombSpec{};
        if (stereo_reverb(&n, 0, 4, &nocombs, &allpasses)) |_| return error.NoCombsSlipped else |e| if (e != error.NoCombs) return error.WrongNoCombs;
        if (!eq(n.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(n.right.samples(), &tr) or n.left.len != n.right.len) return error.NoCombsRefusalMutated;

        var m = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&m, &tl, &tr);
        const many = [_]reverb.CombSpec{.{ .delay = 1, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 }} ** (reverb.max_stages + 1);
        if (stereo_reverb(&m, 0, 4, &many, &allpasses)) |_| return error.TooManySlipped else |e| if (e != error.TooManyStages) return error.WrongTooMany;
        if (!eq(m.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(m.right.samples(), &tr) or m.left.len != m.right.len) return error.TooManyRefusalMutated;

        var d = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&d, &tl, &tr);
        const baddelay = [_]reverb.CombSpec{.{ .delay = 0, .fb_num = 1, .fb_den = 2 }};
        if (stereo_reverb(&d, 0, 4, &baddelay, &allpasses)) |_| return error.ZeroDelaySlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadDelay) return error.WrongZeroDelay;
        if (!eq(d.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(d.right.samples(), &tr) or d.left.len != d.right.len) return error.DelayRefusalMutated;

        var g = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&g, &tl, &tr);
        const badgain = [_]reverb.CombSpec{.{ .delay = 1, .fb_num = 4, .fb_den = 4 }};
        if (stereo_reverb(&g, 0, 4, &badgain, &allpasses)) |_| return error.UnityGainSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadGain) return error.WrongUnityGain;
        if (!eq(g.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(g.right.samples(), &tr) or g.left.len != g.right.len) return error.GainRefusalMutated;

        var r = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&r, &tl, &tr);
        if (stereo_reverb(&r, 1, 4, &combs, &allpasses)) |_| return error.BadRangeSlipped else |e| if (e != error.BadRange) return error.WrongBadRange; // start 1 + count 4 > len 4
        if (!eq(r.left.samples(), &tl) or !eq(r.right.samples(), &tr) or r.left.len != r.right.len) return error.RangeRefusalMutated;
    }

    // 3c. THE DEGENERATE LAW — count = 0 (an empty span in the middle) is the identity on both channels; no sample to reverberate.
    {
        var noop = pan.StereoClip{};
        try load_stereo(&noop, &[_]i16{ 8000, -8000, 4000 }, &[_]i16{ -50, 60, -70 });
        try stereo_reverb(&noop, 1, 0, &combs, &allpasses); // empty span — identity
        if (!eq(noop.left.samples(), &[_]i16{ 8000, -8000, 4000 })) return error.ZeroCountLeftChanged;
        if (!eq(noop.right.samples(), &[_]i16{ -50, 60, -70 })) return error.ZeroCountRightChanged;
    }

    print("GREEN ales-stereo-reverb: the REVERB CARRIED INTO STEREO — ALES186's Schroeder network " ++
        "(wet = series_allpass(sum of parallel combs(dry))) run on BOTH channels with the SAME comb-and-allpass bank, each channel " ++
        "reverbed through ITS OWN network, the wing's keystone made stereo. ALES186 seated the mono reverb; a reverb is heard in a room " ++
        "and a room has two ears, so this is the natural carry, exactly as the stereo comb, the stereo multi-tap, and the stereo allpass " ++
        "were carried before it. The same bank on both channels, each reverberating its own audio, is the linked stereo reverb: both " ++
        "reverberant tails settle in lockstep, the image held; the combs and allpasses are sample counts and named fractions the caller " ++
        "names, so the same bank on each channel gives each ear the same room; mono reverb runs every comb on a copy of its own clip and " ++
        "diffuses its own sum, so run once per channel the left reverberates the left's audio and the right the right's, never crossed — " ++
        "no cross-channel read. Honestly noted: like the echo, flanger, and allpass and unlike the snapshot rungs, the reverb reads its " ++
        "delayed OUTPUT through a @divTrunc recirculation, so an exact panned ratio does NOT survive; the image law proven is the " ++
        "identical-channel one. It validates the whole bank and span once against the shared length before either channel is touched " ++
        "(NoCombs, TooManyStages, BadDelay, BadGain, BadRange; ALES186's precheck reused), so a refusal never reverbs one channel and " ++
        "leaves the other torn; ReverbError reused whole. THE STEREO REVERB LAW: each channel equals ALES186's mono reverb with the same " ++
        "bank byte for byte, the channels genuinely differing. THE IDENTICAL-CHANNEL IMAGE LAW: a centred master staying identical. THE " ++
        "SILENCE / BALANCE / ATOMICITY / DEGENERATE LAW: silence to silence on both, left.len == right.len after, an empty bank / an " ++
        "over-long bank / a bad delay / a bad gain / an out-of-range span each refusing by name with both channels untouched and " ++
        "balanced, count = 0 the identity on both. Purely local — two bounded i16 Clips, each reverbed through the proven mono network, " ++
        "the delays counts of sample indices not milliseconds and the fractions named not coefficients in seconds; no cross-channel " ++
        "read, no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no real speaker\n", .{});
    return 0;
}

pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !u8 {
    _ = init;
    return run_selftest();
}
